==English==

===Verb===
{{en-verb|*}}

# {{lb|en|intransitive}} To [[become]] less [[excited]], [[intense]], or [[angry]].
#: '''''Calm down''' before you hurt somebody.''
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[cause]] to become less excited, intense, or angry.

====Synonyms====
* {{sense|to become less excited}} {{l|en|be still my heart}}, {{l|en|chill}}, {{l|en|chill out}}, {{l|en|chillax}}, {{l|en|pull in one's horns}}, {{l|en|relax}}, {{l|en|unwind}}
* {{sense|to cause become less excited}} {{l|en|chill out}}, {{l|en|relax}}, {{l|en|hose down}}, {{l|en|cool one's jets}}, {{l|en|slow one's roll}}

